 "title": "Drifting Pad",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a pad whose tone wanders on its own, never the same twice: the filter drifting from one random place to the next.\n\nHow it's built: a Clock ticks every bar; a Sample & Hold takes a random value on each tick; a Slew turns the jumps into slow, two-second glides; that drives the Ladder filter's CUTOFF. Two saws, slow attack, Chorus, Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: hold chords for a while.\n\nTweak: the Slew's times (shorter glides become steps), which clock output ticks the Sample & Hold, the filter's CV.",
